# add plugin dependencies for moodle-ci via https://moodlehq.github.io/moodle-plugin-ci/CLI.html#add-plugin
# file support — one dependency per line, format: SPEC [BRANCH]
#   SPEC = owner/repo → passed as the positional project arg
#   SPEC = anything containing ://, ending in .git, or starting git@ → passed via --clone
#  BRANCH is optional per line; when present, adds --branch BRANCH
#  -prefixed lines and blank lines are skipped
#moodlehq/moodle-plugin-something
#moodlehq/moodle-plugin-other MOODLE_502_STABLE
#https://github.com/someuser/moodle-plugin-x.git
#git@github.com:someuser/moodle-plugin-y.git develop
